# S21: Onboarding + Demo Mode

## Objective

First-time user experience. Demo mode: pre-seeded chats/epics/boards (no auth
required) accessible at `?demo=true` or `/demo`. Step-by-step walkthrough overlay
guides user through: send message → ROOT proposes epics → Accept → Open gate →
Run task → see timeline. Public showcase for the platform.

## Features

- **Demo seed script**: `scripts/seed-demo.ts` — creates fixed chat + epic + board
- **Demo mode flag**: `?demo=true` shows seed data, disables auth redirect
- **Walkthrough overlay**: 5-step tooltip chain (UStepIndicator or custom)
- **Setup wizard**: first-time org config (org name, app selection, AI provider key)
- **Public `/demo` route**: no login, read-only (Run is gated behind "Try it" button)

## Tasks

- [ ] S21-T01-FreezeInvariants.pd
- [ ] S21-T02-DemoSeed.pd               — seed script, demo flag middleware
- [ ] S21-T03-WalkthroughOverlay.pd     — 5-step tooltip chain component
- [ ] S21-T04-SetupWizard.pd            — first-run org config UI
- [ ] S21-T05-PublicDemoRoute.pd        — /demo page, read-only, CTAs
- [ ] S21-T06-EmptyStates.pd            — empty state for new chat list, empty board
- [ ] S21-T07-KnowledgeUpdate.pd        — onboarding slug (new)
- [ ] S21-T08-TestsSmoke.pd

## Definition of Done

- [ ] `?demo=true` shows pre-seeded data without auth
- [ ] Walkthrough guides new user through full loop
- [ ] Setup wizard completes: org name saved to organization config
- [ ] `/demo` route publicly accessible (no 401)
- [ ] `bun run test` green (seed script deterministic)

